<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tissamaharama</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mahagama</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tissamaharama is a town in Hambantota District in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, identified with Mahagama, the capital of the ancient kingdom of Ruhuna. The chronicles say it was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanaga">Mahanaga</a> in the 3rd century BCE, and excavations have revealed an early urban settlement. The great Tissamaharama stupa and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tissa-wewa">Tissa Wewa</a> reservoir survive from its early history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tissamaharama.jpg" alt="Tissamaharama" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Krankman · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tissamaharama_dagoba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
